       "content": {
        "id": "v2-proposal-j3-025907-root",
        "type": "question",
        "label": null,
        "prompt": "Sketch these parabolas by taking out a common factor, then CTS. Show vertex and intercepts.",
        "children": [
         {
          "id": "v2-proposal-j3-025907-j3-gp-a",
          "type": "part",
          "label": "a",
          "prompt": "$y=2x^2-4x-6$",
          "answerSpaceMm": 90,
          "answer": {
           "short": "$y=2(x-1)^2-8$; concave up. Vertex $(1,-8)$; $x$-intercepts $(-1,0)$ and $(3,0)$; $y$-intercept $(0,-6)$.",
           "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}y&=2(x^2-2x-3)\\\\y&=2(x^2-2x+1-1-3)\\\\y&=2((x-1)^2-4)\\\\y&=2(x-1)^2-8\\end{align*}$$\nSince $a=2>0$, the parabola is concave up.\n\nLet $x=0$: $y=2(0-1)^2-8=-6$.\n\nLet $y=0$:\n$$\\begin{align*}2(x-1)^2-8&=0\\\\(x-1)^2&=4\\\\x-1&=\\pm2\\\\x&=-1\\text{ or }3\\end{align*}$$\nThe vertex is $(1,-8)$.",
           "solutionDiagrams": [
            {
             "id": "v2-proposal-j3-025907-j3-gp-a-graph",
             "format": "tikz",
             "widthMm": 49,
             "code": "\\begin{tikzpicture}[x=0.6cm,y=0.2cm,>=stealth]\n\\definecolor{curveBlue}{HTML}{268CFF}\n\\path[use as bounding box] (-3,-12) rectangle (5.2,14);\n\\draw[<->,line width=0.5pt] (-2.5,0)--(4.7,0) node[right] {$x$};\n\\draw[<->,line width=0.5pt] (0,-10)--(0,13) node[above] {$y$};\n\\draw[<->,line width=0.8pt,curveBlue,domain=-2.2:4.2,samples=100] plot (\\x,{2*(\\x-1)^2-8});\n\\node[below left] at (-1,0) {$-1$};\n\\node[below right] at (3,0) {$3$};\n\\node[below left] at (0,-6) {$-6$};\n\\node[below right] at (1,-8) {$(1,-8)$};\n\\end{tikzpicture}"
            }
           ]
          }
         },
         {
          "id": "v2-proposal-j3-025907-j3-gp-b",
          "type": "part",
          "label": "b",
          "prompt": "$y=3x^2+12x+18$",
          "answerSpaceMm": 90,
          "answer": {
           "short": "$y=3(x+2)^2+6$; concave up. Vertex $(-2,6)$; no $x$-intercepts; $y$-intercept $(0,18)$.",
           "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}y&=3(x^2+4x+6)\\\\y&=3(x^2+4x+4-4+6)\\\\y&=3((x+2)^2+2)\\\\y&=3(x+2)^2+6\\end{align*}$$\nSince $a=3>0$, the parabola is concave up.\n\nLet $x=0$: $y=3(0+2)^2+6=18$.\n\nLet $y=0$:\n$$\\begin{align*}3(x+2)^2+6&=0\\\\(x+2)^2&=-2\\end{align*}$$\nA real square cannot be negative, so there are no $x$-intercepts.\n\nThe vertex is $(-2,6)$.",
           "solutionDiagrams": [
            {
             "id": "v2-proposal-j3-025907-j3-gp-b-graph",
             "format": "tikz",
             "widthMm": 45,
             "code": "\\begin{tikzpicture}[x=0.6cm,y=0.15cm,>=stealth]\n\\definecolor{curveBlue}{HTML}{268CFF}\n\\path[use as bounding box] (-5.5,-4) rectangle (2,25);\n\\draw[<->,line width=0.5pt] (-5,0)--(1.5,0) node[right] {$x$};\n\\draw[<->,line width=0.5pt] (0,-3)--(0,23) node[above] {$y$};\n\\draw[<->,line width=0.8pt,curveBlue,domain=-4.2:0.2,samples=100] plot (\\x,{3*(\\x+2)^2+6});\n\\node[left] at (0,18) {$18$};\n\\node[below] at (-2,6) {$(-2,6)$};\n\\end{tikzpicture}"
            }
           ]
          }
         },
         {
          "id": "v2-proposal-j3-025907-j3-gp-c",
          "type": "part",
          "label": "c",
          "prompt": "$y=2x^2-16x+20$",
          "answerSpaceMm": 95,
          "answer": {
           "short": "$y=2(x-4)^2-12$; concave up. Vertex $(4,-12)$; $x$-intercepts $(4-\\sqrt6,0)$ and $(4+\\sqrt6,0)$; $y$-intercept $(0,20)$.",
           "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}y&=2(x^2-8x+10)\\\\y&=2(x^2-8x+16-16+10)\\\\y&=2((x-4)^2-6)\\\\y&=2(x-4)^2-12\\end{align*}$$\nSince $a=2>0$, the parabola is concave up.\n\nLet $x=0$: $y=2(0-4)^2-12=20$.\n\nLet $y=0$:\n$$\\begin{align*}2(x-4)^2-12&=0\\\\(x-4)^2&=6\\\\x-4&=\\pm\\sqrt6\\\\x&=4\\pm\\sqrt6\\end{align*}$$\nThe vertex is $(4,-12)$.",
           "solutionDiagrams": [
            {
             "id": "v2-proposal-j3-025907-j3-gp-c-graph",
             "format": "tikz",
             "widthMm": 72,
             "code": "\\begin{tikzpicture}[x=0.7cm,y=0.1cm,>=stealth]\n\\definecolor{curveBlue}{HTML}{268CFF}\n\\path[use as bounding box] (-1.5,-20) rectangle (8.8,27);\n\\draw[<->,line width=0.5pt] (-0.8,0)--(8,0) node[right] {$x$};\n\\draw[<->,line width=0.5pt] (0,-15)--(0,25) node[above] {$y$};\n\\draw[<->,line width=0.8pt,curveBlue,domain=-0.2:8.2,samples=100] plot (\\x,{2*(\\x-4)^2-12});\n\\node[above right] at ({4-sqrt(6)},0) {$4-\\sqrt6$};\n\\node[above left] at ({4+sqrt(6)},0) {$4+\\sqrt6$};\n\\node[below left] at (0,20) {$20$};\n\\node[below] at (4,-12) {$(4,-12)$};\n\\end{tikzpicture}"
            }
           ]
          }
         }
